  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Persisted before the answer",
      "items": [
        "the use case writes the job and answers; the work is not done inside the event listener",
        "the alarm tick is the only thing that starts a drain, and it survives the worker being terminated",
        "navigator.locks keeps one drain at a time when several ticks overlap"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "At least once, made safe",
      "items": [
        "an event can be delivered twice and the worker can die mid-flight: the job id is the idempotency key",
        "a non-idempotent call carries an idempotency key so a retry is safe",
        "the ack is the last write; without it the job is claimed again — which is the point"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Where the failures go",
      "items": [
        "network, 429 and 5xx: exponential backoff with jitter, honouring Retry-After, then the next tick claims it again",
        "a terminal failure goes to the dead-letter store with a visible count",
        "the diagnostics export shows the queue depth, the dead-letter count and the failures — no tokens, no page content"
      ]
    }
  ]
